  "explanation": "A cardiac flatline (asystole) means there is no electrical activity in the heart. Defibrillation only works for shock‑able rhythms (ventricular fibrillation or pulseless ventricular tachycardia) where chaotic electrical signals can be reset. Since asystole has no activity to reset, a shock will not help. The recommended treatment is high‑quality CPR (with appropriate ACLS medications), not defibrillation.",
